{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "ARCHITECH API",
    "version": "0.4.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "ARCHITECH team (ACM Projects, UT Dallas)",
      "url": "https://github.com/acm-projects/ARCHITECH"
    },
    "description": "API for the ARCHITECH Next.js app. All routes live under `frontend/app/api`.\n\n## Data storage: PostgreSQL\nAll user data is stored in **PostgreSQL** through Prisma (`@auth/prisma-adapter`, schema in `frontend/prisma/schema.prisma`):\n\n| Table | Written by | Holds |\n|---|---|---|\n| `users` | `POST /api/auth/register`, Google/GitHub first sign-in, `PATCH /api/users/me` | name, email, bcrypt password hash, experience level, avatar |\n| `accounts` | Google/GitHub sign-in (Prisma adapter) | linked provider id and OAuth access/refresh tokens |\n| `projects` | `PUT /api/projects/{id}` (the canvas syncs automatically) | saved diagrams: title, mode, and the graph as `jsonb` (docs/graph-spec.md) |\n| `component_types`, `component_implementations` | `npx prisma db seed` | the component library and the technologies behind each component |\n\nSign-in itself is stateless (`session.strategy: \"jwt\"`, required for email/password logins). After sign-in the\nbrowser holds only a signed login token (the `next-auth.session-token` cookie) containing the user's id and\nexperience level, never the user record itself. Every protected route takes the id from that token and reads or\nupdates the user in PostgreSQL. The experience level in the token is re-read from PostgreSQL at sign-in and\nwhenever the frontend calls `update()`. (Because of the JWT strategy, the `sessions` table exists but is not used.)\n\n## Routes\n- **Custom:** `POST /api/auth/register`, `PATCH /api/users/me`, `GET /api/github/repos`, `GET /api/projects`, `GET`/`PUT`/`DELETE /api/projects/{id}`\n- **NextAuth v4** (`app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`): everything else under `/api/auth/*`, with\n  Credentials (email + password), Google and GitHub providers. The sign-in page is `/`.\n\n## Calling protected routes\nSign in at http://localhost:3000 in the same browser first. Pages under `/dashboard/*` and `/workspace/*`\nredirect to `/` without a valid login token (`proxy.ts`).\n"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "http://localhost:3000",
      "description": "Local dev server (npm run dev)"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Registration",
      "description": "Email/password account creation"
    },
    {
      "name": "Users",
      "description": "The signed-in user's profile"
    },
    {
      "name": "GitHub",
      "description": "Data from the user's linked GitHub account"
    },
    {
      "name": "Projects",
      "description": "Saved architectures (diagrams) of the signed-in user"
    },
    {
      "name": "NextAuth",
      "description": "Built-in NextAuth endpoints (sign-in, sign-out, session)"
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/auth/register": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Registration"
        ],
        "operationId": "registerUser",
        "summary": "Create an email/password account",
        "description": "Validates the input, normalizes the email (trimmed and lowercased), checks for an existing\nuser case-insensitively, hashes the password with bcrypt and inserts a row into the PostgreSQL `users` table.\nDoes **not** sign the user in; the frontend then calls the credentials sign-in.\n",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RegisterRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "User created",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Message"
                },
                "example": {
                  "message": "User created."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Validation failed or the email is already in use",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "examples": {
                  "invalidBody": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Invalid request body."
                    }
                  },
                  "shortName": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Name must be at least 2 characters."
                    }
                  },
                  "badEmail": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Enter a valid email address without spaces."
                    }
                  },
                  "shortPassword": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Password must be at least 6 characters."
                    }
                  },
                  "duplicate": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Email already in use."
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Server error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Server error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/users/me": {
      "patch": {
        "tags": [
          "Users"
        ],
        "operationId": "updateMyExperienceLevel",
        "summary": "Save the signed-in user's experience level",
        "description": "Called at the end of onboarding step 1. Updates `users.experienceLevel` in PostgreSQL.\nAfter this succeeds, the frontend calls NextAuth's\n`update()`, which re-reads the level into the session token.\n",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ExperienceLevelUpdate"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Level saved",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ExperienceLevelUpdate"
                },
                "example": {
                  "experienceLevel": "Intermediate"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Body is not JSON or the level is not one of the allowed values",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "examples": {
                  "invalidBody": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Invalid request body."
                    }
                  },
                  "badLevel": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Select a valid experience level."
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Database update failed",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Unable to save your experience level."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/github/repos": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "GitHub"
        ],
        "operationId": "listMyGithubRepos",
        "summary": "List the signed-in user's 3 most recently updated GitHub repos",
        "description": "Reads the GitHub OAuth access token from the user's `github` row in the PostgreSQL `accounts` table and calls\n`GET https://api.github.com/user/repos?sort=updated&per_page=3`. The GitHub response is passed\nthrough unchanged, so each item is a full GitHub repository object; only common fields are listed below.\n",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Array of GitHub repository objects",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GithubRepo"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Not signed in, or the GitHub token expired",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "examples": {
                  "notSignedIn": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Authentication required."
                    }
                  },
                  "githubExpired": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "GitHub authorization expired. Reconnect GitHub."
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The user has not connected GitHub",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Connect your GitHub account to access repositories."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "A GitHub account is linked but has no stored access token",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "The linked GitHub account has no access token. Reconnect GitHub."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "GitHub failed or returned an invalid response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "GitHub could not retrieve repositories."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/csrf": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "getCsrfToken",
        "summary": "Get a CSRF token",
        "description": "Required in the body of every NextAuth POST (sign-in, sign-out).",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "CSRF token (also sets the `next-auth.csrf-token` cookie)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "csrfToken": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/providers": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "listProviders",
        "summary": "List configured sign-in providers",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Map of provider id to provider info. Keys are `google`, `github` and `credentials`.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Provider"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/session": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "getSession",
        "summary": "Get the current session",
        "description": "Returns `{}` when signed out. `user.id` and `user.experienceLevel` are added by the `session` callback.",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The session, or an empty object when signed out",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Session"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/callback/credentials": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "signInWithCredentials",
        "summary": "Sign in with email and password",
        "description": "This is what `signIn(\"credentials\", {...})` posts to. Get `csrfToken` from `/api/auth/csrf` first.\n\nServer steps (`authorize` in route.ts):\n1. Rejects a missing or malformed email or password.\n2. Normalizes the email (trimmed and lowercased) and looks up the user in PostgreSQL `users`, case-insensitively.\n3. Rejects users with no `passwordHash` (Google/GitHub-only accounts).\n4. Compares the password with the stored bcrypt hash.\n5. On success, issues the login token with the user's `id` and `experienceLevel` (read from PostgreSQL).\n\nEvery failure returns the same message, \"Invalid email or password\", so the response never reveals\nwhether an email is registered. With `json=true` the error comes back in `{ url }` as `?error=...`;\n`signIn(..., { redirect: false })` surfaces it as `result.error`.\n",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "csrfToken",
                  "email",
                  "password"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "csrfToken": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "email": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "email"
                  },
                  "password": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "format": "password"
                  },
                  "callbackUrl": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "example": "/dashboard"
                  },
                  "json": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "example": "true",
                    "description": "Return JSON `{ url }` instead of a redirect"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "JSON `{ url }` when `json=true`"
          },
          "302": {
            "description": "Redirect to callbackUrl (success) or the error page"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/signin/{provider}": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "startOAuthSignIn",
        "summary": "Start an OAuth sign-in (Google or GitHub)",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OAuthProvider"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "csrfToken"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "csrfToken": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "callbackUrl": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "example": "/dashboard"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "302": {
            "description": "Redirect to the provider's consent screen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/callback/{provider}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "oauthCallback",
        "summary": "OAuth callback (called by Google or GitHub, not by the app)",
        "description": "Register these as the redirect URIs in the Google and GitHub OAuth app settings:\n`http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google` and `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/github`.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/OAuthProvider"
          },
          {
            "name": "code",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "state",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "302": {
            "description": "On first sign-in the Prisma adapter inserts a row into PostgreSQL `users` (name, email, image)\nand one into `accounts` (provider id and OAuth tokens). Later sign-ins reuse them.\nSets the login token and redirects to callbackUrl.\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/auth/signout": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "NextAuth"
        ],
        "operationId": "signOut",
        "summary": "Sign out",
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "csrfToken"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "csrfToken": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "callbackUrl": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "example": "/"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "302": {
            "description": "Clears the session cookie and redirects"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/projects": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "operationId": "listProjects",
        "summary": "List the signed-in user's projects",
        "description": "Every project of the signed-in user, most recently changed first. Stored in the PostgreSQL `projects` table, one row per project with the diagram in a `jsonb` column.",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The user's projects",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "projects": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Database error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Unable to load your projects."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/projects/{id}": {
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "id",
          "in": "path",
          "required": true,
          "description": "Project id, generated by the browser (UUID). Letters, digits, '-' and '_', at most 100 characters.",
          "schema": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,100}$"
          },
          "example": "ce8672d2-cc09-4e77-a3f3-767458b9c36a"
        }
      ],
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "operationId": "getProject",
        "summary": "Get one project",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The project",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No project with this id belongs to the user (another user's project is also reported as not found)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Project not found."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Database error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Unable to load the project."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "operationId": "saveProject",
        "summary": "Create or replace a project",
        "description": "Creates the project with this id, or replaces it if the user already has it. The browser generates the id, so creating offline and retrying a failed save are both safe: sending the same project twice stores it once.\n\nThe diagram is validated against docs/graph-spec.md (section 5): known component types, labels of 1-60 characters, unique node and edge ids, edges between existing nodes, no self-connections or repeated connections, settings within each component's range, and `data.implementation` must exist and belong to the node's type. At most 500 nodes and 2,000 edges.\n\nThe canvas calls this automatically: every change is synced in the background.",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProjectInput"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Replaced an existing project",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "201": {
            "description": "Created a new project",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid id or body. The message names the first problem and where it is.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "examples": {
                  "badType": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "graph.nodes[0].data.type \"firewall\" is not a known component type."
                    }
                  },
                  "dangling": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "graph.edges[0].target must be the id of a node in this graph."
                    }
                  },
                  "selfLoop": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "graph.edges[0] connects a node to itself."
                    }
                  },
                  "range": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "graph.nodes[1].data.properties.replicas: Replicas must be at most 1000."
                    }
                  },
                  "implementation": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "Implementation \"redis\" is a cache, not a database."
                    }
                  },
                  "title": {
                    "value": {
                      "error": "title must be 1-80 characters."
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "The id belongs to another user's project",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Project not found."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Database error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Unable to save the project."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "tags": [
          "Projects"
        ],
        "operationId": "deleteProject",
        "summary": "Delete a project",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "Deleted"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No project with this id belongs to the user",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Project not found."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Database error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                },
                "example": {
                  "error": "Unable to delete the project."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/github/import": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "GitHub"
        ],
        "operationId": "importGithubRepo",
        "summary": "Build a design from a GitHub repository",
        "description": "Uses the GitHub account the user connected at sign-in (its token in the `accounts` table) to read the repository through GitHub's GraphQL API (`POST https://api.github.com/graphql`): one query for the top-level file list and stack files, and one for the same files in up to 8 top-level folders (monorepos).\n\nStack files read: package.json, docker-compose.yml / compose.yml, prisma/schema.prisma, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml, go.mod, pom.xml, build.gradle.\n\nDetection rules map what they use to components and technologies (for example `next` → Web App (Next.js), `ioredis` → Cache (Redis), `@apollo/server` → API (GraphQL), a `postgres` image → Database (PostgreSQL)), each with its evidence. The design is laid out left to right with typical connections, validated against docs/graph-spec.md and saved as a new project (`source: \"github\"`, opens in free play). Connections are a best guess to adjust on the canvas.\n\nTechnologies the repository uses that ARCHITECH does not model (for example a Traefik or ClickHouse service, or a .NET worker) are returned as `customTechnologies` and saved with the project, so they appear in its sidebar under \"From your repo\" and can be dragged onto the canvas as unmeasured custom components. A repository with only such technologies still imports.",
        "security": [
          {
            "sessionCookie": []
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GithubImportRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "The new project and what was detected.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GithubImportResult"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid owner or repo name.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Not signed in, or the GitHub authorization expired (reconnect GitHub).",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "No GitHub account connected, or the repository was not found / is not visible to the account.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "The linked GitHub account has no access token.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Neither recognizable components nor unmodeled stacks/services were found.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "GitHub is rate-limiting requests.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "GitHub returned an error.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "sessionCookie": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "cookie",
        "name": "next-auth.session-token",
        "description": "NextAuth login token (signed JWT with the user id), set when you sign in. It identifies the user; all user data is read from PostgreSQL."
      }
    },
    "parameters": {
      "OAuthProvider": {
        "name": "provider",
        "in": "path",
        "required": true,
        "schema": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "google",
            "github"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "responses": {
      "Unauthenticated": {
        "description": "Not signed in",
        "content": {
          "application/json": {
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
            },
            "example": {
              "error": "Authentication required."
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "ExperienceLevel": {
        "type": "string",
        "enum": [
          "Beginner",
          "Intermediate",
          "Advanced"
        ]
      },
      "RegisterRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "name",
          "email",
          "password"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 2,
            "description": "Trimmed before saving",
            "example": "Shivam"
          },
          "email": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "email",
            "maxLength": 254,
            "description": "Trimmed and lowercased; no spaces",
            "example": "shivam@example.com"
          },
          "password": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "password",
            "minLength": 6,
            "example": "hunter22"
          }
        }
      },
      "ExperienceLevelUpdate": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "experienceLevel"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "experienceLevel": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ExperienceLevel"
          }
        }
      },
      "Message": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "message": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "Error": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "error": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "Provider": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "google"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "Google"
          },
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "oauth",
              "credentials"
            ]
          },
          "signinUrl": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "callbackUrl": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "Session": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "user": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "User id (cuid)"
              },
              "name": {
                "type": "string",
                "nullable": true
              },
              "email": {
                "type": "string",
                "nullable": true
              },
              "image": {
                "type": "string",
                "nullable": true
              },
              "experienceLevel": {
                "allOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ExperienceLevel"
                  }
                ],
                "nullable": true,
                "description": "null until onboarding step 1 is completed"
              }
            }
          },
          "expires": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        }
      },
      "GithubRepo": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Subset of GitHub's repository object (the full object is returned)",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "ARCHITECH"
          },
          "full_name": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "acm-projects/ARCHITECH"
          },
          "private": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "html_url": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "uri"
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string",
            "nullable": true
          },
          "language": {
            "type": "string",
            "nullable": true
          },
          "default_branch": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "main"
          },
          "stargazers_count": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "updated_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "owner": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "login": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "avatar_url": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "uri"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "GraphNode": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "id",
          "type",
          "position",
          "data"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "One component on the canvas (React Flow node). See docs/graph-spec.md section 2.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "example": "database-1"
          },
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "architecture"
            ]
          },
          "position": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "x",
              "y"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "x": {
                "type": "number"
              },
              "y": {
                "type": "number"
              }
            }
          },
          "data": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "type",
              "label"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "type": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Component type name (component_types.name)",
                "enum": [
                  "client",
                  "web-app",
                  "mobile-app",
                  "cdn",
                  "dns",
                  "server",
                  "api-gateway",
                  "api",
                  "load-balancer",
                  "database",
                  "cache",
                  "queue",
                  "worker",
                  "object-storage",
                  "search",
                  "auth",
                  "custom"
                ]
              },
              "label": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1,
                "maxLength": 60,
                "example": "Orders DB"
              },
              "implementation": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "component_implementations.id of the chosen technology; omitted means the type's default",
                "example": "postgresql"
              },
              "properties": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "User overrides, e.g. replicas, capacity, cacheHitRate, authCheckRate, searchRate. Ranges per component type in docs/graph-spec.md section 4.",
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "oneOf": [
                    {
                      "type": "string",
                      "maxLength": 200
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "number"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "boolean"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "example": {
                  "replicas": 2
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "GraphEdge": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "id",
          "source",
          "target"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A connection, pointing in the direction requests flow.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "server-1->database-1"
          },
          "source": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "server-1"
          },
          "target": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "database-1"
          },
          "sourceHandle": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "targetHandle": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      "GraphDocument": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "nodes",
          "edges"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A saved diagram, as defined in docs/graph-spec.md.",
        "properties": {
          "schemaVersion": {
            "type": "integer",
            "enum": [
              1
            ]
          },
          "nodes": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 500,
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GraphNode"
            }
          },
          "edges": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 2000,
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GraphEdge"
            }
          },
          "customTechnologies": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 30,
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomTechnology"
            },
            "description": "Optional. Technologies from an imported repository that the app does not model."
          }
        }
      },
      "ProjectInput": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "title",
          "mode",
          "graph",
          "createdAt",
          "updatedAt",
          "lastOpenedAt"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Body of PUT /api/projects/{id}. An `id` field may be included but must match the URL.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 80,
            "example": "Shop"
          },
          "mode": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "learn",
              "challenge"
            ]
          },
          "learnSkipped": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false
          },
          "source": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "blank",
              "duplicate",
              "template",
              "shared",
              "github"
            ]
          },
          "graph": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GraphDocument"
          },
          "createdAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "updatedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time",
            "description": "When the title or diagram last changed"
          },
          "lastOpenedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        }
      },
      "Project": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "id",
          "title",
          "mode",
          "learnSkipped",
          "graph",
          "createdAt",
          "updatedAt",
          "lastOpenedAt"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "ce8672d2-cc09-4e77-a3f3-767458b9c36a"
          },
          "title": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 80,
            "example": "Shop"
          },
          "mode": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "learn",
              "challenge"
            ]
          },
          "learnSkipped": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false
          },
          "source": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "blank",
              "duplicate",
              "template",
              "shared",
              "github"
            ]
          },
          "graph": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/GraphDocument"
          },
          "createdAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "updatedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time",
            "description": "When the title or diagram last changed"
          },
          "lastOpenedAt": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        }
      },
      "DetectedComponent": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "nodeId",
          "label",
          "type",
          "technology",
          "evidence"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "nodeId": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The node it became in the project's graph.",
            "example": "database-1"
          },
          "label": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "PostgreSQL"
          },
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Component type (component_types.name).",
            "example": "database"
          },
          "technology": {
            "type": "string",
            "example": "PostgreSQL"
          },
          "evidence": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "example": [
              "backend/package.json uses \"pg\"",
              "docker-compose.yml runs the \"postgres\" image"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "GithubImportRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "owner",
          "repo"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "owner": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "GitHub user or organization.",
            "example": "octocat"
          },
          "repo": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Repository name.",
            "example": "shop"
          }
        }
      },
      "GithubImportResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "project",
          "detected",
          "scannedFiles",
          "customTechnologies"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "project": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Project"
          },
          "detected": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DetectedComponent"
            }
          },
          "scannedFiles": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Stack files that were read.",
            "example": [
              "backend/package.json",
              "docker-compose.yml"
            ]
          },
          "customTechnologies": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CustomTechnology"
            },
            "description": "Unknown docker-compose services and app folders in stacks the app does not model (.NET, Rust, Ruby, PHP, Elixir, C++). Also saved in project.graph.customTechnologies."
          }
        }
      },
      "CustomTechnology": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "id",
          "name",
          "evidence"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "A technology from an imported repository that ARCHITECH does not model. Listed in the project's sidebar under \"From your repo\"; dragged onto the canvas it becomes a `custom` node (`data.properties.technology` = name) that Run Design passes traffic through without measuring.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,59}$",
            "example": "traefik"
          },
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 60,
            "example": "Traefik"
          },
          "evidence": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 5,
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 200
            },
            "example": [
              "docker-compose.yml runs the \"traefik\" image"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
